WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.880
Hi, I'm Semih. This is Zecured: borrow against shielded ZEC. Only the proof crosses.

00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:06.940
No bridge. No wrapped token. No single custodian.

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:11.540
So using it in DeFi means giving up that privacy. $2.7 million is borrowed against ZEC today,

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:13.460
through a custodian, in public.

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:17.260
DeFi for shielded ZEC. Zecured is DeFi for shielded ZEC. Borrow USDC on Morpho against

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:20.260
it, or swap into it. No bridge. No wrapped token.

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:24.980
Your ZEC sits in a fresh three-of-five FROST vault. No single key exists, and a theft slashes the

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:27.030
signers.

00:00:27.030 --> 00:00:28.830
Only one proof crosses to Base.

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:32.550
A RISC Zero proof shows the deposit is in a Zcash block that Base verified itself.

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:33.550
Only that proof crosses.

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:38.990
Here it is, live. This is our home page: you can borrow here, you can swap into

00:00:38.990 --> 00:00:43.670
ZEC here, and you can see your loans here. This is a real Morpho Blue

00:00:43.670 --> 00:00:47.190
market: you can see the borrow rate and the supply. And here is what's real

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:50.590
and what's a mock. Now I'll show you how it works. This is our borrow tab,

00:00:50.590 --> 00:00:57.200
you choose the amount of ZEC here, and I'll lock 0.05 ZEC.

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:00.880
The loan's key lives only in my browser. I save a backup, download it, and continue.

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:04.960
This is my vault's shielded Ironwood address. Any Zcash wallet can pay it by scanning this QR code,

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:08.760
so we built our own Ironwood wallet, and our demo wallet pays the vault: a real shielded

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:13.360
payment on Zcash testnet. And we are waiting... done. Now we wait about ten minutes

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:19.040
for confirmations on Zcash. It now has ten confirmations on Zcash. A GPU makes a RISC Zero proof

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:24.370
that my payment is in a Zcash block. My address and my transaction stay private. And after

00:01:24.370 --> 00:01:28.890
about three minutes: proven on Base. RISC Zero's verifier on Base accepts the proof. All done, and

00:01:28.890 --> 00:01:33.850
here you can see the transaction hash. Now we have zZEC, and we can borrow against

00:01:33.850 --> 00:01:41.730
it. As you can see, we deposited 0.05 ZEC, and I borrow 10 USDC, and you

00:01:41.730 --> 00:01:45.670
can see the health factor and the collateral right here. Create the account.

00:01:45.670 --> 00:01:50.350
A brand-new account borrows test USDC. Its gas is sponsored: it never held any ETH.

00:01:50.350 --> 00:01:54.910
We just borrowed 10 USDC, and you can see the transaction hash. This is our loan page:

00:01:54.910 --> 00:01:58.750
you can see the health, the utilization and the LTV here. You can close or repay

00:01:58.750 --> 00:02:03.950
from here, borrow more, or withdraw part of the collateral,

00:02:03.950 --> 00:02:08.510
reduce the debt, protect your position, or send USDC to another Base address

00:02:08.510 --> 00:02:14.390
here. Here I choose close from collateral, recommended, and I paste a fresh Ironwood

00:02:14.390 --> 00:02:20.340
address, check this address, and get a market maker's quote. Then we sign and

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:27.060
send it to the market maker. We are waiting for the market maker to close our position.

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:29.940
My ZEC goes back to an address from our own Ironwood wallet. The signers check it,

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:33.900
and Base only sees a salted commitment. A market maker repays my debt and takes its

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:39.780
share in ZEC, and the rest comes back to me, shielded. We are waiting... committed on

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:44.260
Base. Both shares are paid on Zcash, signed by three of the five signers, and confirmed on Base. This is

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:47.940
our swap page. No custodian: your USDC waits on Base until the maker proves, in

00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:53.020
zero knowledge, that it paid your Ironwood address. I enter 5 USDC and get the maker's quote,

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:58.600
and I will receive 0.0039 ZEC.

00:02:58.600 --> 00:03:04.100
Then I connect my wallet and sign

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:09.000
in the wallet. The order is opened,

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:13.910
and we are waiting for the maker. My USDC

00:03:13.910 --> 00:03:17.350
waits in the contract. It is released only when the maker proves, in zero knowledge, that it

00:03:17.350 --> 00:03:21.070
paid my shielded address. We wait about ten minutes for the payment to be proven on Base.

00:03:21.070 --> 00:03:24.390
The swap settled. The maker paid my shielded address on Zcash and proved it on Base, in

00:03:24.390 --> 00:03:28.750
zero knowledge. Only then did the contract release my USDC. Base sees my wallet and the order,

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:34.780
never where the ZEC went. No custodian. No bridge. And I can show you: it's finished,

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:38.100
the loan closed from collateral. This is our market page: you can see the total

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:41.260
supply, total borrow, the borrow rate, what lenders earn, and the details here. Everything

00:03:41.260 --> 00:03:45.620
you just saw ran live, with real transactions on Zcash testnet and Base Sepolia. Proving needs

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:49.660
